{title: God's Love Outpoured}
{artist: Larry Holder}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 80}

Verse 1
This song has been arranged for guitar, flute, and clarinet, in hopes of playing

Verse 2
this at church in the near future with my daughters, who play the latter two instruments.

Verse 3
It can also be played simply with guitar, which plays throughout all verses.

Verse 4
God's Love Outpoured
Words & Music by Lawrence Keith Holder
Copyright (c) 1997 Lawrence Keith Holder

Verse 5
1. God's love outpoured at Bethlehem,
As He came down to live as men
And draw our sinful souls to Him:
God's love outpoured at Bethlehem!

Verse 6
2. God's love outpoured upon a hill,
Where loaves and fish were made to fill.
God's care for us endureth still:
God's love outpoured upon a hill!

Verse 7
3. God's love outpoured upon the sea,
To calm the storm, from fear to free.
From fear of hell He ransomed me:
God's love outpoured upon the sea!

Verse 8
4. God's love outpoured within a room,
Not long before the cross and tomb,
To us the Bride, from Christ the Groom:
God's love outpoured within a room!

Verse 9
5. God's love outpoured from Calvary:
The Son of God in agony.
Yet death gave way to victory:
God's love outpoured from Calvary!

Verse 10
6. God's love outpours on us today;
His Word is clear to show the Way.
So turn to Him, don't turn away:
God's love outpours on us today!
